codex
I found the round-one miss: the short-height media query did fire and the tab was collapsed, but it was moved vertically using a normal-stack offset while the zoom cluster was overflowing its tiny canvas containing block. I’m correcting the reproduction fixture now so the RED test reflects that actual containing-block geometry in Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit before touching production CSS.
