.hermes/planning/responsive-ui-20260724\logs\h2-r3.log:19:4. **NEW-3 ΓÇö NOT RESOLVED.** The dock/zoom vertical reservation and toast relocation are materially improved: `--dock-max-h` covers the expanded form, the zoom cluster is placed 12px above that cap, and S4/S5/S7 own focused collision gates before S8 (`Plan.md:168-197,298-301`). But the synthesis collapsed-tab rectangle is not disjoint from the expanded dock as claimed. At 320px, `--dock-w = 284`, so the right-anchored dock spans x=18..302. The proposed centered tab width is `320 - 2├ù(18+52) = 180`, spanning x=70..250: **180px horizontal overlap**. At 568px the overlap is 308px. The formula reserves only the 52px zoom column, not the dock's up-to-360px rectangle, while both elements are bottom chrome (`Plan.md:175-195`). No separate vertical offset for the collapsed tab is specified. The promised S5 `tab Γê⌐ (dock Γê¬ zoom) = Γêà` gate therefore has no design capable of passing the expanded-dock fixture as written. This is a genuine collision-model contradiction, not implementation-ticket polish.
.hermes/planning/responsive-ui-20260724\logs\h2-r3.log:23:6. **Fresh adversarial pass ΓÇö two genuine defects, no additional blocking scope creep.** NEW-5 and NEW-6 below are the only change-request findings. The proprietary GestureEvent path and tier-3 fallback add justified complexity because pinch is binding; they are not scope creep. The zoom model, per-slice RED ownership, AuthGate coverage, short-height matrix, toast move, dock cap, and real-device pinch escalation are otherwise internally aligned. Non-blocking implementation guidance: encode separate auto-fit modes (`column-auto` versus user-requested `overview-auto`) so resize cannot silently turn an overview Fit into column fit; preserve layout space when simplifying overview cards; and exercise VoiceOver/TalkBack control activation as part of the existing real-device gates.
